, and CFI brand names. It primarily serves retailers, manufacturers, and parcel carriers in the consumer goods, appliances, food products, and automotive industries. The company was founded in 1978 and is headquartered in North Liberty, Iowa.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael J. Gerdin | Chairman of the Board, President & CEO | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $222K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $606 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Heartland Express, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $780M market cap on $806M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $67M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin -5.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 52% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 16% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 33% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Heartland Express, Inc. Announces Participation in Upcoming Conference","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/heartland-express-inc-announces-participation-143300259.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795789980.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.879,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"3 Cash Rich Bank Stocks Built For Higher Rates","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-bpop/popular/news/3-cash-rich-bank-stocks-built-for-higher-